room.description:
Choose independent temperature probes where possible. Rooms sharing a heat-pump head must select the same climate entity. Higher comfort priority wins when rooms disagree; temperature limits take precedence.

If a sensor reports only when its reading changes, select it below as well. Its last value stays usable while Home Assistant shows it available; sensors not selected there still need recent reports. Unknown, unavailable, and invalid readings are always excluded.

{detail}

system.description:
Comfort adjustments normally run every 60–120 seconds. Safety, heartbeat, and recovery checks run separately at the safety interval. Minimum run/off times apply to each head's requested mode; the heat-pump system controls its compressor. Safety can stop a head early. The shared all-off settling interval still applies before changing direction. Confirm equipment timing before enabling live commands, then turn on Controller enabled on the House climate controller device after saving.

Call offsets push active head setpoints past both the room target and the head's own temperature, within equipment limits. External room probes decide when the call ends; your room target stays unchanged. Set an offset to 0 to use the room target directly for that direction.

{detail}

